  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "On the road toward Bai Gu Mountain, Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing scout a house-sized beehive holding a large frenzy needle bee group. Fang Yuan already knows that once those bees become Gu, their piercing can defeat Sky Canopy Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          207
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_bai_gu_mountain",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "char_bai_ning_bing",
          "gu_sky_canopy_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "After the Xuan Yuan Divine Pheasant ruins the nest, Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing take hive pieces to eat. The returning swarm transfers its fury onto them and chases without pause. Bai Ning Bing takes most of the attacks with Sky Canopy Gu; Fang Yuan’s Carapace Gu covers his back. They escape by diving into a lake that washes the hive smell off their bodies. The bees keep diving and resurfacing in shallows, but lose the scent trail.",
        "chapters": [
          208
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "chase-near-bai-gu-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After that chase, Bai Ning Bing’s back is full of fingertip-sized holes; a rank three demonic Gu Master proves a greater threat than the frenzy needle bee itself.",
        "chapters": [
          209
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "chase-near-bai-gu-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_demonic_path"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "No cited chapter shows a Gu Master refining or owning Frenzy Needle Bee Gu. The swarm on the Bai Gu Mountain road is a wild insect group.",
        "chapters": [],
        "certainty": "inferred",
        "confidence": "C",
        "verification": "no_citation",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "chase-near-bai-gu-mountain",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_master"
        ]
      }
    ]
